{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 389540, "name": "Adam Williamson", "username": "adamwill", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/adamwill/{size}/377_2.png", "created_at": "2025-03-18T22:55:37.576Z", "cooked": "<h2><a name=\"p-389540-problem-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-389540-problem-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Problem</h2>\n<p>The Fedora logo on the Fedora 42 Beta login screen for the GNOME desktop (Fedora Workstation) may appear unusually large (and pixelated). This only happens if “fractional scaling” is in use (this depends on your display size and resolution).</p>\n<h2><a name=\"p-389540-cause-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-389540-cause-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Cause</h2>\n<p>Not yet known.</p>\n<h2><a name=\"p-389540-related-issues-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-389540-related-issues-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Related Issues</h2>\n<p>Bugzilla report: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/2346088\">#2346088</a></p>\n<h2><a name=\"p-389540-workarounds-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-389540-workarounds-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Workarounds</h2>\n<p>As this is an entirely cosmetic issue, no workaround is necessary.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 4, "updated_at": "2025-04-14T12:06:27.890Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 343, "reads": 77, "readers_count": 76, "score": 1760.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 147275, "topic_slug": "fedora-logo-on-gnome-login-screen-is-very-large", "display_username": "Adam Williamson", "primary_group_name": "qa", "flair_name": "qa", "flair_url": "bug", "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 77, "badges_granted": [], "version": 3, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/2346088", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "2346088 – Fedora logo is